---
title: "delete_object_with_dynamic_fields (Sui Move Concepts: Orphaned Dynamic Fields)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_fields: check if object has dynamic fields defined
    q_check_fields --> q_has_fields: dynamic fields exist on object
    q_check_fields --> q_safe_delete: no dynamic fields
    q_has_fields --> q_check_collection: check if object is Table or Bag
    q_check_collection --> q_check_empty: is Table or Bag collection
    q_check_collection --> q_allow_delete: is plain object with dynamic fields
    q_check_empty --> q_safe_delete: collection is empty (count == 0)
    q_check_empty --> q_abort: collection is non-empty
    q_allow_delete --> q_delete: object::delete(id) - fields become orphaned
    q_delete --> [*]: object deleted, dynamic fields permanently inaccessible

    q_safe_delete --> q_delete_safe: object::delete(id)
    q_delete_safe --> [*]: object safely deleted

    q_abort --> [*]: abort - cannot delete non-empty Table/Bag

    note right of q_allow_delete
        INV-001: Deleting object with dynamic fields makes fields permanently inaccessible
        INV-002: Field values may be non-drop, causing permanent lock of assets
        INV-003: No runtime protection for plain objects - only Table/Bag have count guards
    end note

    note right of q_check_empty
        INV-004: Table and Bag track entry count to prevent accidental deletion
        INV-005: Unbounded collections should always use Table/Bag, not raw dynamic fields
    end note
